CORRECTION, written after the run. THE DEPLOY SUCCEEDED; THE GATE THAT
STOPPED THE SCRIPT WAS WRONG, AND IT WAS MY INPUT THAT WAS WRONG.
======================================================================

WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED. All three resources were PATCHed, one PublishXml
covered all three, and all three read back byte-identical. The server
stamps were then read and all five agreed: app.js APP_BUILD 22d065d93a,
app.js canonicalised and hashed 22d065d93a, styles.css 4993f5eee9, and the
HTML referencing both. The build on the org is the intended one.

The script then re-counted this wave's fingerprints in the SERVER copy and
exited on one of the three app symbols. That symbol is multi-line and I
joined it with LF.

WHY THAT IS WRONG, and it is the exact mirror of the defect the previous
wave hit in the stylesheet half. The app half of PRE-FLIGHT 3b counts the
raw `git show` blob, which git hands back with LF endings. The SAME symbol
map is counted again after the push against the SERVER copy, which is the
working tree's bytes and is CRLF. One spelling cannot satisfy both. An
LF-joined symbol passes 3b and then fails the server re-check on a build
that is perfectly correct.

MEASURED, against the stamped local app.js whose sha256 the read-back
already proved identical to the org copy (9355d8b0e2cd6472):

  the failing symbol, joined LF    0   <- what the gate asked for
  the same symbol,   joined CRLF   1   <- what the bytes actually carry

  and in those same shipped bytes:
    TO BE FILLED     0
    Delivered by     0
    Update cadence   0
    ds-dict-gap      0

So the server copy carries this wave. The other two app symbols and the
stylesheet symbol passed the server re-check unaided; only the multi-line
one failed, and only on its line endings.

THE SCRIPT IS ARCHIVED EXACTLY AS IT RAN. It is the record of what was
done, so it is not edited after the fact. The correction belongs here.

FOR THE NEXT COPY OF THIS SCRIPT, and this is the part that must not be
lost: the comment above TICKET_SYMBOLS in the archived file says an
LF-joined symbol is correct for the app half. It is correct for 3b and
wrong for the server re-check. Either normalise both sides to CRLF, or
keep every app symbol single-line, which is what every wave before this
one did and why the trap had not surfaced.

NOTHING WAS ROLLED BACK AND NOTHING NEEDED TO BE. The snapshot of the
previous build was committed and pushed as 7d3778e before the first PATCH,
and it remains the rollback for 0067415e4f + e6de22bc37.

